doorman Debian package
======================

The package installs the daemon, CLI, PAM module, default config template,
runtime models, and systemd units. It intentionally does not edit PAM
configuration.

After installing:

1. Enroll and test:

   doorman enroll "$USER"
   doorman test "$USER"

2. Only after the test path works, add the PAM line for the services you want:

   auth    sufficient    pam_doorman.so

For Sway, the package ships an optional adapter in:

   /usr/lib/doorman/adapters/sway/doorman-sway-lock

It prefers gtklock when available and falls back to swaylock. Include the
example binding from:

   /usr/lib/doorman/adapters/sway/sway.conf.example

The package creates /etc/doorman/doorman.toml from the template only when it is
missing. Keep a root shell open while editing PAM. Removing the package
preserves /var/lib/doorman. Purging the package removes /etc/doorman,
/var/lib/doorman, and the doorman system user.
